Again, thank you gemini for helping developed this AIDA model.

We know what AIDA model doing is that we have background file (previous 6 hour forecast) Xb,
and observations both at t0, the AIDA is to start Xb, by some progress, or AI training,
so we get Xa, which is the new Analysis at t0, which fit better to observations.

Now, we what to move forward a step to change this model to a forecast model.
Let us start with X-6 (Analysis at previous 6 hours), X0 (current Analysis).
From historical data, we have O+6 (observation at future 6 hours),
through AI process using X-6, X0, and O+6 to get X+6, where X+6 fit O+6 better.

After training, we get a checkpoints file .chpt, using this file, and X-6, X0, we get X+6,
then apply X0, X+6, we get X+12, and so on to get a forecast model.

The difference of this model, is that traditional AI weather models use X to train models,
and then use X to do forecast. Our model use not only X, but also Obs to train the model,
and then use X to do forecast.

Could you please help me, Gemini? By changing our background data .zarr file
to a analysis background data .zarr file?
